  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Medical Laboratories (NAICS 621511) federal obligations total $87.9M for FY2027 to date. The market shows 249 awards with an average award size of $353K, and obligations fell 69.4% year over year. Annual history shows a FY22 high of $1.7B, followed by $418M in FY23, $398M in FY24, $460M in FY25, and $287M in FY26. The current-year total is partial because the fiscal year is not complete. Buyers are concentrated, led by the Department of Veterans Affairs with $88.7M in obligations, followed by the Department of Justice with $581K and the Department of State with $19.8K. Vendors concentrate most obligations among a few large laboratory providers, with QUEST DIAGNOSTICS INCORPORATED and LABORATORY CORPORATION OF AMERICA combining for the majority of FY2027 to date obligations. Contracting officers and industry teams should treat the FY2027 total as a year-to-date snapshot, not a full-year figure.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How did obligations change year over year?",
